      "widgets_values": [
        "2b2-DUALRES - BUILD THE SfM DATASET (low-res poses + 8K pinhole faces)\n\nReplaces the old 2b2 (which OOMed: loading 324 x 8K into one ComfyUI tensor = ~122 GB).\nHere the SfM runs on the LOW-RES panoramas/ (fits, ~4 GB) and the pinhole cube faces are\nreprojected from the 8K panoramas_upscaled/ read straight off disk.\n\nWIRING (both folders are pointed at DIRECTLY -- no Resolve node, because once SfM has run\nonce the dataset marker flips to 'spheresfm_colmap' and Resolve would look for cube faces).\n1. Load LOW-RES panoramas: set the loader 'directory' to <dataset>/panoramas (1440x720),\n   select_every_nth = 1.\n2. SphereSfM Dataset (Dual-Res): pano_frames_1 <- the low-res loader; hires_dir = the 8K\n   panoramas_upscaled folder; output_name = the dataset name.\n\nMATCHER = exhaustive  -> matches ALL frame pairs so the separate WAN trajectories can fuse\ninto ONE model (sequential only linked temporally-adjacent frames -> 4 disconnected models).\nON_SPLIT = stop  -> if it STILL forms >1 model, the node raises with the per-model frame\nbreakdown and reprojects nothing, so you can see the trajectories didn't merge. Set it to\n'largest' to train on the biggest model anyway.\n\nhires_dir must contain the SAME frames as the low-res set, in the SAME sorted order\n(panoramas/frame_00000.png <-> panoramas_upscaled/00000.png). face_size = 0 keeps full 8K\ndetail (faces scaled from the rescaled 8K SPHERE camera).\n\nAfter it succeeds, train in LichtFeld (pinhole, NO --gut):\n  LichtFeld-Studio.exe -d <dataset> -o <out> --headless --train --strategy mcmc --max-cap 2000000 --sh-degree 2"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
